--
-- Description
-- -----------
-- This tests that the TX packet buffer will stall reading of data when the
-- buffer is already full and this is the second packet in the system.
-- 
-- This tests with a programmed AHB burst length of 16-beats using a 2K RAM.
--
--
--      NOTE: MAX FRAME SIZES ARE AS FOLLOWS:-
--
--       RAM SIZE | 4-BEAT | 8-BEAT | 16-BEAT
--       ------------------------------------
--       2K SRAM  |  2016  |  1984  |  1920
--       4K SRAM  |  4064  |  4032  |  3968
--
--
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- -------------------
-- * Checks TX packet buffer full for 16-beat bursts
-- * Checks HBURST is correctly encoded for 16-beat bursts (checked by tb_dma)
--
--
-- Detailed Test Description
-- -------------------------
-- 1. Check and initialise the relevant registers
-- 2. Transmit a long frame that almost fills the buffer.
-- 3. Transmit a short frame to cause a buffer full half way through 2nd frame
-- 4. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the 
--     above operations were handled properly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------



--******************************************************************************
-- 1. Check and initialise the relevant registers
--******************************************************************************
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      10 00020110  -- set the TX packet buffer RAM to 2K (bit 10), 16-beat
apbwr      00 00000008  -- enable transmit
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbrd      30 00000000  -- check that all interrupts are now enabled
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbwr      04 0000000b  -- 100Meg mode, jumbo frames enabled
apbrd      04 0000000b  -- verify write to speed register..
apbrdf     20 00000000  -- check contents of the receive status register and trigger reception of frame




